  "summary": "I added a \"Tour\" button below the canvas, in the page flow rather than over it. The new code typechecks and builds. The render shows the button under the canvas with no console errors. I did not run a tour in a browser, because the tools can't click. The 3-second timing, the \"Stop tour\" label, the return to the overview and the `touring` field are untested.\n\nClicking the button starts the tour at Mercury and works outward. It spends 3 seconds on each planet, and that time includes the 1.5 s camera move. The info panel shows for each planet. After Neptune it returns to the overview and the button goes back to \"Tour\". While touring the button reads \"Stop tour\", and clicking it ends the tour and returns to the overview.\n\nI made a few choices you didn't specify:\n- A click on a planet, a click on empty space, Escape, `__focusPlanet` and `__unfocus` all cancel a running tour.\n- Pausing doesn't pause the tour timer, because the tour runs on real time.\n- `window.__TASK_STATE__` now has `touring` (boolean)."
